# useful codes the project not depend on

## fastboot_auth

PC-side pairing and unlock tool for the SFB BDS secure fastboot. It talks to
the phone's EFI Boot Mgr app for pairing and drives the regular fastboot
binary for the challenge-response unlock.

```
make -C tools/fastboot_auth

# pair once (the app shows the address and a six-digit code)
fastboot_auth pair 192.168.1.23:37021

# unlock the running BDS for this boot
fastboot_auth auth [-d <serial>] [-f <path to fastboot>]
```

Needs OpenSSL headers and libcrypto. The identity (RSA-2048 key and a
self-signed `CN=user@host` certificate) is kept in `~/.fastboot_auth`; the
phone installs the certificate into `AUTH_CERTS`, which the BDS
reads at boot.
